1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,739
This is a ruin.

2
00:00:02,639 --> 00:00:05,683
It has three rooms and two tunnels,

3
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:10,480
and it's older than anyone who could have built it.

4
00:00:11,380 --> 00:00:13,120
I didn't model it,

5
00:00:13,570 --> 00:00:16,613
and I didn't place a single rock.

6
00:00:17,513 --> 00:00:22,296
All I did was write down where the empty space is.

7
00:00:24,096 --> 00:00:25,835
Today, you write yours.

8
00:00:27,035 --> 00:00:31,817
A ruin is hollow, so what you describe is the hollow.

9
00:00:32,717 --> 00:00:37,935
A chamber is a ball of open space, and that's a room.

10
00:00:38,835 --> 00:00:43,617
A passage is a tube of open space between two rooms,

11
00:00:44,067 --> 00:00:45,807
and that's a tunnel.

12
00:00:46,707 --> 00:00:51,489
A box is a block with flat sides, a built room,

13
00:00:51,939 --> 00:00:55,417
and you'll add one yourself at the end.

14
00:00:57,217 --> 00:01:00,261
And whatever you don't describe is wall.

15
00:01:01,461 --> 00:01:05,374
I go to the very end of the file,

16
00:01:05,824 --> 00:01:08,433
and I start a new section.

17
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:12,811
Its key has to be the word relics,

18
00:01:13,261 --> 00:01:16,739
because that's the word the game looks for.

19
00:01:17,639 --> 00:01:19,813
Then comes the ruin itself,

20
00:01:20,263 --> 00:01:25,046
with a name for people and a key for the file.

21
00:01:25,946 --> 00:01:32,467
And it has one field, called Loc, which is where it stands: across, height, along.

22
00:01:34,267 --> 00:01:37,311
The station is at zero, zero, zero,

23
00:01:37,761 --> 00:01:40,804
and the hulk is nine thousand along,

24
00:01:41,254 --> 00:01:45,602
so this is past the hulk, on the same line.

25
00:01:46,502 --> 00:01:49,980
The sentence underneath is a note to myself,

26
00:01:50,430 --> 00:01:53,039
and no player ever reads it.

27
00:01:54,239 --> 00:02:00,761
Now a room, and it has three hashes, the same as the ruin, not four.

28
00:02:01,661 --> 00:02:04,704
A room isn't written inside the ruin.

29
00:02:05,154 --> 00:02:06,893
It's written beside it,

30
00:02:07,343 --> 00:02:10,387
and this line says whose it is.

31
00:02:11,287 --> 00:02:14,765
That's the ruin's key, and not its name.

32
00:02:16,565 --> 00:02:18,739
Then Chamber, with four numbers.

33
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:23,552
The first three say where, measured from the ruin,

34
00:02:24,002 --> 00:02:27,480
so three zeros is the ruin's own spot.

35
00:02:28,380 --> 00:02:31,424
The fourth is the radius, nine hundred,

36
00:02:31,874 --> 00:02:34,917
so the room is eighteen hundred across.

37
00:02:35,817 --> 00:02:38,426
My ship is about a hundred.

38
00:02:39,626 --> 00:02:44,409
The Nave is three thousand to one side, and it's bigger.

39
00:02:45,309 --> 00:02:47,917
And it has a passage line:

40
00:02:48,367 --> 00:02:50,541
passage to mouth, three fifty.

41
00:02:51,441 --> 00:02:56,224
That's the tunnel, and the word is the other room's key,

42
00:02:56,674 --> 00:02:59,717
and the number is the tunnel's radius.

43
00:03:00,617 --> 00:03:04,096
There's a space between them, and no comma.

44
00:03:05,896 --> 00:03:10,678
I write each tunnel once, on either of its two rooms.

45
00:03:11,578 --> 00:03:15,926
The Vault is twenty-eight hundred further along from the Nave,

46
00:03:16,376 --> 00:03:18,985
with a passage back to it,

47
00:03:19,435 --> 00:03:22,043
so the ruin turns a corner.

48
00:03:23,243 --> 00:03:25,417
With the file in front,

49
00:03:25,867 --> 00:03:30,650
I open the command palette and ask for the Relic Plan.

50
00:03:31,550 --> 00:03:35,028
And there it is, drawn from the file,

51
00:03:35,478 --> 00:03:38,087
and the game isn't even running.

52
00:03:38,987 --> 00:03:43,335
Top looks straight down, and each square is a thousand.

53
00:03:44,235 --> 00:03:48,148
I can hover over a room for its size,

54
00:03:48,598 --> 00:03:51,641
and over a tunnel for its length.

55
00:03:53,441 --> 00:03:58,224
Now I click the Vault, and I make it eight hundred.

56
00:03:59,124 --> 00:04:02,602
Look at the file: one line has changed.

57
00:04:03,502 --> 00:04:07,850
So the picture and the file are the same thing.

58
00:04:08,300 --> 00:04:10,909
I press Undo, and it's back.

59
00:04:12,109 --> 00:04:15,152
The file says what the ruin is.

60
00:04:16,052 --> 00:04:22,574
And this line, which has been in your mission since the day you made it,

61
00:04:23,024 --> 00:04:25,633
builds every ruin the file holds.

62
00:04:26,533 --> 00:04:30,446
It makes the space, it puts rock around it,

63
00:04:30,896 --> 00:04:34,809
and it writes the ruin's name on the map.

64
00:04:35,709 --> 00:04:37,448
You don't touch it.

65
00:04:39,248 --> 00:04:44,030
And if there's no ruin in the file, it does nothing.

66
00:04:45,230 --> 00:04:48,274
So I run lint, and it's clean.

67
00:04:49,174 --> 00:04:53,957
Now I point a passage at a room that doesn't exist,

68
00:04:54,407 --> 00:04:57,450
and lint tells me so, by name.

69
00:04:58,350 --> 00:05:00,959
Read the end of that sentence:

70
00:05:01,409 --> 00:05:07,061
with this one going nowhere, the game doesn't build the ruin at all.

71
00:05:08,861 --> 00:05:11,904
Next, a fourth hash on the Vault.

72
00:05:12,804 --> 00:05:17,152
The plan still shows three rooms, but lint isn't fooled.

73
00:05:17,602 --> 00:05:22,820
It says the room is nested, and the game won't read it.

74
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:28,937
So it's three hashes on the ruin, and three on every room.

75
00:05:30,737 --> 00:05:33,780
And here's one thing lint can't see.

76
00:05:34,680 --> 00:05:39,028
I take the Loc line away, and lint says clean,

77
00:05:39,478 --> 00:05:42,522
because it can't know where I meant.

78
00:05:43,422 --> 00:05:47,770
The ruin would be built on top of the station,

79
00:05:48,220 --> 00:05:49,959
so keep the line.

80
00:05:51,159 --> 00:05:55,941
I start the game with a server and a Helm console.

81
00:05:56,841 --> 00:06:00,320
And there, past the hulk, is The Hollow.

82
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:04,698
That marker is the middle of the Mouth.

83
00:06:06,498 --> 00:06:08,672
And this is my wall.

84
00:06:09,572 --> 00:06:13,485
From inside it looks like a field of rocks,

85
00:06:13,935 --> 00:06:17,848
and it's scenery today, so it won't stop me.

86
00:06:18,748 --> 00:06:23,096
Through the tunnel we go, and this is the Nave.

87
00:06:24,296 --> 00:06:26,035
Now it's your turn.

88
00:06:26,485 --> 00:06:30,398
Add a fourth room, and make it a box,

89
00:06:30,848 --> 00:06:33,457
a built room with flat walls.

90
00:06:34,357 --> 00:06:38,270
Join it by overlapping the room next to it.

91
00:06:39,170 --> 00:06:40,909
Then move it away,

92
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:46,141
and watch lint tell you the ruin is in two pieces.

93
00:06:47,041 --> 00:06:50,520
And then join it again, with a passage.

94
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:56,667
Next time, we decide what these walls are made of.
